{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/992726-hack-going-all-out-on-mage-centrism","id":992726,"title":"Hack: Going all out on Mage-centrism","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-24T20:20:19-07:00","id":992726,"title":"Hack: Going all out on Mage-centrism","content":"I've spent a lot of time trying to force Mage into crossover compatibility and balance, and while I still think that's worthy of doing, I'm beginning to think it would be at least a fun experiment to take things the other way, and posit a world where everything is Mage-centric. <br /> <br /> In this world: <br /> <br /> - The Supernal is the source of all magic, and all supernatural phenomena can ultimately be understood in Supernal terms. <br /> - The specific tone is focused less on archetypes of monstrosity and more on dark mystery, espionage/intrigue, and adventure. <br /> - All supernatural creatures are connected to the Supernal in some way. For example, the True Fae are there, but Arcadia is either definitely an Emanation realm, the same as Mage Arcadia, or something else. <br /> - Some of the other splats exist as minor templates that mages can possess, or as legacies. For example, vampires and changelings both exist, but they are much less powerful, as they lack Disciplines or Contracts. They can, however, Awaken as mages with some inherent powers and a tendency towards certain types of magic. <br /> <br /> Making mages even more flexible would be nice here as well, because if they're the only splat, then there's no problem of overlap, and they're free to cover all the ground they want.<br /> <br /> I admit it does have a fair bit of influence from Genius and Ascension. For example, Genius allowed you to be an Inspired Mane, and in Ascension you could be an artificial being. The problem with letting homunculi and androids awaken in Awakening, of course, is that you start getting thematic overlap with Promethean, and if you have mages with horns and green skin because they're actually physical embodiments of old superstitions you're treading on changeling's turf. But if we put it all in The World of Mana, we don't have to worry about that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-24-2016, 11:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T20:32:35-07:00","id":992733,"title":"","content":"Making Mage <i>more </i>flexible might be pretty hard actually. There's fairly little a Mage, given the right arcana, can't accomplish. The only thing I can think of is to make it so that instead of getting dots in arcana, you instead buy Practices. So lets say you choose to gain the Practice of Perfecting, you can now perfect all aspects of reality, be it something that would fall under Forces, Death, Space, whatever. Of course, some would likely be prerequisites to others, like needing to know Fraying before learning Unraveling, though you could theoretically throw even that out and just lump all of Fraying and Unraveling under Unmaking and have them be one thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T20:41:27-07:00","id":992738,"title":"","content":"Hm, I admit that I'm not entirely sure what it would entail, I was talking more in the general sense of if we make all the other splats subsets of Mage cosmology, a Mage should ultimately be able to master any part of the magical landscape. I'm thinking of folding in some form of path flexibility to accommodate this. And, of course, letting mages be mad scientists. <br /> <br /> I'm liking this idea more and more. Here's another thing I've realized: the high power level of Mage means that you can have some template stacking without wrecking the game. Letting players play a Mage who's also a vampire or an android doesn't unbalance things too much when you consider the stuff mages can do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T22:32:19-07:00","id":992784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/992726-hack-going-all-out-on-mage-centrism#post992726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- The Supernal is the source of all magic, and all supernatural phenomena can ultimately be understood in Supernal terms.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think most mages (and a number of Mage players <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) already see the setting in these terms. Vampires are some kind of lower depth being or some by product of the Death Arcanum. Prometheans are some kind of creature born of madness and interaction with the Aether etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/992726-hack-going-all-out-on-mage-centrism#post992726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- The specific tone is focused less on archetypes of monstrosity and more on dark mystery, espionage/intrigue, and adventure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tone is something that is very difficult to do with a Hack other than saying, &quot;this is the tone of this hack&quot; and providing description of the sorts of games you envision occurring within it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/992726-hack-going-all-out-on-mage-centrism#post992726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- All supernatural creatures are connected to the Supernal in some way. For example, the True Fae are there, but Arcadia is either definitely an Emanation realm, the same as Mage Arcadia, or something else.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I said above, while this may not literally be true from our point of view, within the Mage setting, I think the majority of Mages view the World of Darkness through a lens of seeing the Supernal as the influence behind everything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/992726-hack-going-all-out-on-mage-centrism#post992726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Some of the other splats exist as minor templates that mages can possess, or as legacies. For example, vampires and changelings both exist, but they are much less powerful, as they lack Disciplines or Contracts. They can, however, Awaken as mages with some inherent powers and a tendency towards certain types of magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here I'm not sure what I can add really other than rewriting every other splat to &quot;nerf&quot; them would be a lot of work. Since mages with some arcanum under their belt are already very powerful, have you considered just upping the starting Gnosis to say 3 and giving out 10 dots of Arcanum at the beginning of the Chronicle.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/992726-hack-going-all-out-on-mage-centrism#post992726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Making mages even more flexible would be nice here as well, because if they're the only splat, then there's no problem of overlap, and they're free to cover all the ground they want.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, not sure what to add here. Mages are already incredibly versatile and become more so as they gain more arcanum. If you mean thematically, I'm also not sure what to add. Depending on the ST and the chronicle they're running, Mage can be run with a focus on investigating mysteries, confronting horror, falling into a spiral of growing hubris and madness etc. already.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T22:49:27-07:00","id":992791,"title":"","content":"About the adjusting splats to minor templates, I'd be willing to put in the work to turn them into Merits or Legacies or something like that. Genius handles Manes as a Merit, so I'd go with something like that. <br /> <br /> Just giving mages more power isn't what I'm looking for. I'm looking for a way to incorporate other supernatural beings into a game that is assumed to be entirely Mage-centric by default. And I fully admit that I'm just doing it because I think it would be cool to have mages that are ogres or goblins or androids. <br /> <br /> For example, while the ultimate outcome is up to debate, I like the idea of doing away with Prometheans and instead having a wider category of magically-created beings. The Unbidden has an artificial human created by a Mage, so I'm talking about replacing Prometheans with various Mage-made artificial beings. <br /> <br /> And yeah, this is aimed at Mage fans. With Mage, there's the urge to use it to explain all the other splats under that umbrella, but fans of those splats often take issue to that. I'm torn between the two: I think it's cool to make a whole coherent setting based entirely on the Supernal mythology, but I also love the other settings and don't want to overshadow them. This is meant to be a way to handle that, to create a codified Supernal-only setting to be Mage's playground. And while a lot of mages might see everything as Supernal, you kind of end up with the dilemma of saying either &quot;no, they're arrogant dicks who're trying to force everything under their umbrella&quot; or &quot;yes, they're right, everything else is part of the Supernal&quot;. This is a way to employ the second possibility without having to overshadow the other lines.<br /> <br /> And I don't think tone is that difficult to indicate. Mage already indicates a particular sort of tone, although there's plenty of room for change. All this would do is emphasize that, and emphasize how it differs from, say, Blue Book or any of the other lines, and how bringing everything under the Supernal umbrella changes things. <br /> <br /> About &quot;versatility&quot;, I was talking more about more options for atypical paths and mad science.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T23:39:38-07:00","id":992813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gullinbursti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/992726-hack-going-all-out-on-mage-centrism?p=992784#post992784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think most mages (and a number of Mage players <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) already see the setting in these terms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most mages in the base game recognize that the vast majority of magical phenomena are several degrees removed from their slice of occult experience; most magic is Phenomenal in origin by virtue of the simple fact that it doesn't have to travel as far, metaphysically speaking.<br /> <br /> I think the main thing to do if you're aiming to present the notion of the Supernal and/or the Abyss as the root of all things magical is to play up Verges, mess with the consequences of summoned Supernal entities staying past their deadline, and generally make ample use of visible buffers linking Supernal phenomena to Phenomenal specimens \u2014 there need not be straight-up vampire-Legacies for there to be connective tissue between Specters and vampirism when you can introduce proxy-vectors akin to the Strix.<br /> <br /> Play up the expansiveness of the cosmology the Awakened are made aware of and the lengths to which pursuit of a Mystery can take them. Make use of the game's established threshold-beings to increase the proliferation of mages who've been subverted by some alien god or another, whether it be from poking around the wrong corners of the Anima Mundi or eating the wrong spirit-meat during an esoteric ritual in the Shadow.<br /> <br /> Extend logically the implications of the tale of the Annunaki \u2014 Supernal magic is unclean power on its best behavior, putting on a pleasant face to keep the average observer from cottoning to how easily its destructive heritage comes to the fore, and there's so much that seems like it <i>could be</i> just outside the soap-bubble of coherent reality\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T23:48:16-07:00","id":992819,"title":"","content":"Yeah, there's going to be a lot of that. A lot of existing setting elements will remain, they'll just be firmly established as Emanation Realms or Verges. <br /> <br /> And wow having the Strix as Supernal or Abyssal is a really cool idea. <br /> <br /> I'm not pushing the &quot;mages are awful cursed monstrous doomed madmen etc etc&quot; thing as much here, and it's not so much a tonal hack as a setting one. The tone is very much in line with Mage canon: occult mysteries and power struggles for reality. <br /> <br /> Would it be possible to represent the various possibilities as merits? I'm thinking of &quot;mythic origin&quot; or &quot;arcane origin&quot; as an umbrella term for a Mage who's also another type of supernatural being. So, there would be a set of mythic origin merits, for things like dhampir, vampires, changelings, artificial beings, and so on, with options (and plenty of downsides!) for each. <br /> <br /> I think I'd make it so that Awakened vampires aren't as hurt by the sun. It still hurts them and weakens them, but they can go out in it if they're covered up or using some kind of magical defense.<br /> <br /> That's why I like this idea, really. It means I can have daywalking Supernal-magic using vampires without wrecking Requiem's themes and setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T23:55:16-07:00","id":992823,"title":"","content":"The thing is, mages are Hubristic and colour what they come across with their own preexisting knowledge. For example, I can't remember if it was just his own games canon, but I believe DaveB used the Strix as an example of a Lower Depth entity. I believe the aspect of reality (or supernal symbol) they were missing was Vitae/Blood. Mages, like most people who believe themselves to very clever, categorize things and ignore or mislabel things they don't understand. A ghost is scary, a &quot;a non-repeating phantasm, or a class-5 free roaming vapor&quot; is something that's routine and involves paper work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T00:04:33-07:00","id":992830,"title":"","content":"Well, this is assuming a universe where mages are right, and all supernatural phenomena ultimately come from the Supernal or related parts of Mage cosmology. That doesn't mean that mages can't face reality-bending weirdness that defies explanation: with the Abyss and the Lower Depths, you have plenty of Weird Shit, and you can adapt other entities to fit the Mage cosmology while still leaving them massively dangerous and mysterious: the Gentry, the Idigam, the Machine, and so on could all be incorporated. And you could always say &quot;this thing comes from another reality where the rules are completely different&quot;. There's plenty of room for things impossible to categorize and so on.<br /> <br /> There's also no longer a Mage supremacy issue or a crossover issue, because it's a self contained universe where Mage supremacy is the point, and other supernatural beings are less powerful but can learn Supernal magic. <br /> <br /> Does anyone have any ideas for how to incorporate major splats? <br /> <br /> Here's what I have so far:<br /> <br /> - Vampires don't have clans or Disciplines, but they have some basic powers and weaknesses and can Awaken. <br /> - Werewolves are a Legacy of Thyrsus mages who patrol the spirit world. <br /> - Prometheans are reinterpreted as the many kinds of artificial life a Mage could potentially create. These artificial beings can potentially Awaken. <br /> - Changelings are people kidnapped by the Gentry, who are explicitly Supernal entities similar in power and role to archmasters (and archmasters could theoretically abduct someone and turn them into a changeling). Changelings only get seeming and kith blessings (some of which are changed to provide bonuses to different types of magic), no contracts. <br /> - Sin-Eaters are a Legacy of Moros who returned from the verge of death by Awakening. <br /> - Mummies are a Legacy of liches, maybe? They use Supernal magic instead of their canon powers. <br /> - Deviants are handled via a Mythic Origin that represents the Mage being the result of some sort experiment that permanently altered them. <br /> - Beasts are, I don't know, Abyssal or Lower Depthsy?<br /> - The only Angels or Demons are Supernally-derived or lower depths entities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-25-2016, 03:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T00:27:49-07:00","id":992837,"title":"","content":"What about the different fuel stats? You should probably make everything different flavours of Mana. <br /> <br /> As for the splats... I have ideas. Maybe ditch Paths as is. Mages have the usual template abilities (Mage Sight, Attainments, etc) and potential access to all Arcana. Each other splat has its base template abilities, but limited access to Arcana (only 1-3, maybe being unable to over reach):<br /> <br /> Vampires: Mind and Death<br /> <br /> Werewolves: Life and Spirit<br /> <br /> Changelings: Fate, Time and Mind<br /> <br /> Geist: Death<br /> <br /> Prometheans: Matter and Forces<br /> <br /> etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T00:37:37-07:00","id":992840,"title":"","content":"Hm, that's a cool idea too! But I do kind of prefer the &quot;merit&quot; idea, and keeping paths, but opening them up to more variation. But I do think I might steal the idea of giving Mythic Origins limits on what magic they can use. Maybe it influences their ruling and inferior arcana?<br /> <br /> My idea for the other splats is that they don't need fuel stats, because they don't have their own specific powers (disciplines, etc) but only have innate powers (spending blood for physical attributes, kith blessings, etc) and Supernal magic. The Uratha Legacy doesn't have need Essence, because their shapeshifting and powers come from the Life and Spirit powers they already have. <br /> <br /> I'd also love Legacy suggestions! I'm actually probably ditching the supervillain legacy. A bit too gonzo and cartoony for what I'm going for (AKA, the original tone of Awakening, which I'm trying to stay true to). But Legacy ideas are welcome! Here are some I've had, from other threads and here:<br /> <br /> - The Uratha<br /> - The Sin-Eaters<br /> - Adamantine Arrow luchadores<br /> - Adamantine Arrow equilibrium-style gun duelists. <br /> - A knightly order based on magical powered armor. Constructing pieces of the armor corresponds to a mage's advancement. When a Mage joins, an image of their armor appears as their nimbus, and they fill it in with actual physical items. Their base is a massive astral UFO that functions as a flying cathedral. <br /> - The Virtual Adepts as a free council legacy of cyberpunk hackers and street samurai. <br /> - Silver Ladder clockwork mages seeking to create an orderly utopia with cosmic machinery. <br /> - Their Mysterium Acanthus counterparts, who focus on using the image of the clockwork to understand time and fate. <br /> - The Foils, and Acanthus legacy that deliberately take on antagonistic roles to spur their &quot;nemeses&quot; to greater glories. <br /> - A legacy that believes in a force called the Wyrd, and becoming increasingly attuned to Fate, eventually becoming True Fae. <br /> <br /> Maybe we could adapt some of the covenants, refinements, lodges, etc as Legacies?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T00:49:02-07:00","id":992841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/992726-hack-going-all-out-on-mage-centrism?p=992840#post992840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My idea for the other splats is that they don't need fuel stats, because they don't have their own specific powers (disciplines, etc) but only have innate powers (spending blood for physical attributes, kith blessings, etc) and Supernal magic. The Uratha Legacy doesn't have need Essence, because their shapeshifting and powers come from the Life and Spirit powers they already have.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd actually recommend keeping Essence as a fuel trait, mainly because a big way to lend credibility to the idea of Supernal origins is to allow those entities to naturalize themselves into the Phenomenal World or make things whose magic works on those derived principles; it also lets the dichotomy between Essence-using entities and Mana-using entities be meaningful.<br /> <br /> Like, for real, &quot;it's a Legacy&quot; is not going to be a terribly satisfying origin for the vast majority of gameline-having supernaturals in this setup without functionally reinventing the wheel to make a force that acts for all intents and purposes like the primordial entities underlying those games' metaphysics. Allow divergent evolution to come into play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T00:52:51-07:00","id":992843,"title":"","content":"Well, I kind of am reinventing the wheel, and saying that all of those entities are clearly and directly Supernal (or Abyssal). Explicitly saying &quot;The God-Machine was built by the Seers to control humanity&quot; is an example of what I'm talking about. Like, making werewolves a legacy isn't meant to replace werewolf. Making werewolves a legacy is done to let someone playing Awakening be a werewolf, while also throwing in some references and connections to the main ChroD universe. If you start introducing more and more supernatural forces, you get the ChroD canon as it already is. And while there's nothing wrong with that, this project is about having fun with making Awakening its own universe. <br /> <br /> But I do think I'll keep Essence as a fuel trait for spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T02:43:47-07:00","id":992862,"title":"","content":"What if Essence is the &quot;Fallen&quot; representation of Mana?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T02:54:53-07:00","id":992864,"title":"","content":"That's a cool idea! I think I'll go with that. <br /> <br /> God damn it, Thorbes, you are killing me here, seeing your avatar always cheers me up. How am I supposed to maintain my reputation as a bitter spiteful misanthrope with that adorable snake around? /sarcasm<br /> <br /> Anyway, here's another Legacy idea: Sarkicists, a Thrysus legacy based on the creepy flesh cultists from the SCP verse. They worship disease, pain, fear, monstrosity, and mutation. Oh, and they're also among the nicest factions in the setting. That doesn't mean it's W40K grimdark- plenty of factions are at least conditionally nice. But the Sarkicists really are nice. You know those idealized churchy small town bake sale communities that don't actually exist? The Sarkicists are like that, but with more limbs and more organic weapons that spray acid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T03:06:17-07:00","id":992867,"title":"","content":"Something to keep in mind is that if you change the setting so that everything falls under the purview of the Supernal then it can all be analyzed with Mage Sight to solve any mystery about it. Even without crossover default Mage doesn't have that because it's assumed that most mysteries are not in fact originating from the Supernal (Hence the Supernal mystery book in the making).<br /> <br /> So you might want to think through the implications of that. Maybe remove Mage Sight altogether so there's actually stuff left to investigate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T03:19:50-07:00","id":992871,"title":"","content":"Hm, good point. I'd definitely have to sit down with the mechanics and work that out. Though the fact that there's a book about Supernal mysteries means that entirely Supernal things can in fact be mysteries. And then there's the Abyss and the Lower Depths...<br /> <br /> Alright, I have an idea for mummies that I really like! They're a kind of extremely powerful Reaper that can only be created through mass sacrifice of a large number of souls. While it's much harder to get away with in modern times, performing the Rite isn't impossible, which gives you plenty of hooks, mainly preventing it from being performed again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-25-2016, 04:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}